# Environment of the standalone app (`hermes atlas serve`, `python -m hermes_atlas serve` or
# `atlas-intelligent-ui serve`), for a shell or a service unit. Inside Hermes, Atlas reads these
# through the profile's secret scope, so nothing here is needed. It lives in docs/ on purpose:
# Hermes copies every *.example at the root of a plugin to its real name when installing it.

# The Hermes API server that the Atlas chat talks to (default: http://127.0.0.1:8642/v1, with
# /p/<profile> added for a secondary profile).
ATLAS_HERMES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8642/v1
# Its bearer key. Falls back to API_SERVER_KEY, the key Hermes's own API server uses.
ATLAS_HERMES_API_KEY=

# The Hermes profile whose library Atlas opens (default: ~/.hermes, or %LOCALAPPDATA%\hermes).
# HERMES_HOME=/path/to/hermes/profile
# Keep the canvas library somewhere else (default: <HERMES_HOME>/plugin-data/atlas-intelligent-ui).
# ATLAS_DATA_DIR=/path/to/atlas-data
